      <Placemark>
        <name>17 Starigrad town</name>
        <description><![CDATA[opis: Coordinates: 43.18454 N, 16.5947 E<br>Wind Protection: Protected from all winds and waves<br>Starigrad town is a beautiful town located on the north west center side of Hvar Island. Very well protected and one of the most beautiful towns in Split sailing region. Starigrad is one of the oldest towns in Croatia, with a history that dates back to Greek and Roman times. Beautiful spot to wander the streets and have a unique insight on Roman and Greek times. There are moorings on the north and south sides of the town: the north side is better protected from north winds and much easier to dock with strong NE winds.<br>Services available: Electricity, Water, Showers, Restrooms, Market, Restaurant & Bar<br>Reservation: No official reservation. First come, first serve policy. <br>VHF channel: 9<br><br><br>name: <br>description: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1681-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="opis">
            <value><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43.18454 N, 16.5947 E
Wind Protection: Protected from all winds and waves
Starigrad town is a beautiful town located on the north west center side of Hvar Island. Very well protected and one of the most beautiful towns in Split sailing region. Starigrad is one of the oldest towns in Croatia, with a history that dates back to Greek and Roman times. Beautiful spot to wander the streets and have a unique insight on Roman and Greek times. There are moorings on the north and south sides of the town: the north side is better protected from north winds and much easier to dock with strong NE winds.
Services available: Electricity, Water, Showers, Restrooms, Market, Restaurant & Bar
Reservation: No official reservation. First come, first serve policy. 
VHF channel: 9

]]></value>
