      <Placemark>
        <name>Duboka Bay</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Coordinates: 43° 9.80' N, 16° 22.48' E<br>Sea bed: Sand and Seagrass (mixed bottom)<br>Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW<br>Depth: Not specified<br><br>Serene and peaceful bay on Hvar island with good shelter and easy anchoring. Mixed bottom of sand and seagrass - note that the west side of the bay has no sand (land lines recommended there). Beach accessible by dinghy. Can be quite lonely even in peak season. Caution: Open bay suffers from wave motion of passing ferries and hydrofoils. Wasps are a significant problem, especially in summer! Bonus: A local lady sometimes comes by dinghy selling local wine and olive oil.<br>naziv: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 9.80' N, 16° 22.48' E
Sea bed: Sand and Seagrass (mixed bottom)
Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW
Depth: Not specified

Serene and peaceful bay on Hvar island with good shelter and easy anchoring. Mixed bottom of sand and seagrass - note that the west side of the bay has no sand (land lines recommended there). Beach accessible by dinghy. Can be quite lonely even in peak season. Caution: Open bay suffers from wave motion of passing ferries and hydrofoils. Wasps are a significant problem, especially in summer! Bonus: A local lady sometimes comes by dinghy selling local wine and olive oil.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="naziv">
            <value/>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.3822326,43.163543,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Palmižana</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Coordinates: 43° 9.53' N, 16° 23.87' E<br>Sea bed: Sand, Rocks, Seagrass<br>Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW<br>Depth: ~5m<br><br>A haven of peace on Saint Clement Island (Pakleni Islands) near Hvar. Anchor on sandy bottom with shore lines - very good grip in mud and seagrass. Crystal clear water ideal for swimming with fish. Easy Mediterranean-style mooring. Small grocery store at the marina ~1.5km away (nice walk along the coast). Restaurants in Palmižana cove. Caution: Rocks are razor sharp when setting shore lines. Bay is somewhat exposed - beware of wind and swell. Some daytime swell from passing motorboats and RIBs.<br>naziv: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 9.53' N, 16° 23.87' E
Sea bed: Sand, Rocks, Seagrass
Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW
Depth: ~5m

A haven of peace on Saint Clement Island (Pakleni Islands) near Hvar. Anchor on sandy bottom with shore lines - very good grip in mud and seagrass. Crystal clear water ideal for swimming with fish. Easy Mediterranean-style mooring. Small grocery store at the marina ~1.5km away (nice walk along the coast). Restaurants in Palmižana cove. Caution: Rocks are razor sharp when setting shore lines. Bay is somewhat exposed - beware of wind and swell. Some daytime swell from passing motorboats and RIBs.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="naziv">
            <value/>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.3977889,43.1589844,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
