      <Placemark>
        <name>Smričevica</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Coordinates: 43° 1.07' N, 16° 9.75' E<br>Sea bed: Rocks and Seagrass (sand patches in center)<br>Wind Protection: Sheltered from N, NE, E, W, NW<br>Depth: ~11m in center of bay<br><br>Absolutely beautiful anchorage on Vis island with wonderful crystal clear water. Anchor in the center of the bay where sandy patches exist - use plenty of chain (40-45m recommended) as holding can be weak. Lines ashore required. Small pebble beach and a few uninhabited houses. Caution: Overhanging rocks on the sides - risk of anchor getting stuck under rocks; keep to center. Space is limited and fills up quickly in season. Note: A local owner may charge ~20€ for tying lines to the rocks.<br>naziv: Smricevica Beach]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 1.07' N, 16° 9.75' E
Sea bed: Rocks and Seagrass (sand patches in center)
Wind Protection: Sheltered from N, NE, E, W, NW
Depth: ~11m in center of bay

Absolutely beautiful anchorage on Vis island with wonderful crystal clear water. Anchor in the center of the bay where sandy patches exist - use plenty of chain (40-45m recommended) as holding can be weak. Lines ashore required. Small pebble beach and a few uninhabited houses. Caution: Overhanging rocks on the sides - risk of anchor getting stuck under rocks; keep to center. Space is limited and fills up quickly in season. Note: A local owner may charge ~20€ for tying lines to the rocks.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="naziv">
            <value>Smricevica Beach</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.1621328,43.0180145,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Plaža Gradac</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Coordinates: 43° 4.55' N, 16° 8.18' E<br>Sea bed: Sand and Rocks<br>Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW (excellent from NE winds and swells)<br>Depth: Deep (lines ashore needed)<br><br>Beautiful and silent anchorage on Vis island. Excellent protection from NE winds and swells. Fairly deep water requiring lines ashore. Very peaceful - expect solitude with perhaps only local fishermen dropping nets in the morning. Limited reviews available.<br>naziv: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 4.55' N, 16° 8.18' E
Sea bed: Sand and Rocks
Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW (excellent from NE winds and swells)
Depth: Deep (lines ashore needed)

Beautiful and silent anchorage on Vis island. Excellent protection from NE winds and swells. Fairly deep water requiring lines ashore. Very peaceful - expect solitude with perhaps only local fishermen dropping nets in the morning. Limited reviews available.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="naziv">
            <value/>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.1366047,43.0758307,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Uvala Salbunara</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Coordinates: 42° 59.13' N, 16° 0.12' E<br>Sea bed: Sand and Rocks (seaweed on sides)<br>Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW<br>Depth: ~5m<br><br>Fantastic narrow bay on Biševo island near Komiža (Vis). Anchor on sandy bottom in ~5m depth with 35m chain and two lines ashore - aim well as there's a lot of seaweed on the sides. Small jetty on the north side where the island ferry docks twice daily. Gorgeous sandy beach at the head of the bay. Great sunsets. Caution: Rocks on shore are very sharp when securing lines. Bonus: Nadja at the small guesthouse on the beach sells local dessert wine.<br>naziv: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Coordinates: 42° 59.13' N, 16° 0.12' E
Sea bed: Sand and Rocks (seaweed on sides)
Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW
Depth: ~5m

Fantastic narrow bay on Biševo island near Komiža (Vis). Anchor on sandy bottom in ~5m depth with 35m chain and two lines ashore - aim well as there's a lot of seaweed on the sides. Small jetty on the north side where the island ferry docks twice daily. Gorgeous sandy beach at the head of the bay. Great sunsets. Caution: Rocks on shore are very sharp when securing lines. Bonus: Nadja at the small guesthouse on the beach sells local dessert wine.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="naziv">
            <value/>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.0026903,42.9861491,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Medvidina špilja</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Coordinates: 42° 57.55' N, 16° 0.98' E<br>Sea bed: Sand<br>Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW<br>Depth: ~15m<br><br>Incredible anchorage on Biševo island featuring the spectacular Medvidina špilja (Monk Seal Cave) - a real alternative to the crowded Blue Grotto with free entry! Anchor in about 15m on sand with turquoise water. Explore the very large, very deep cave by dinghy or paddle - it gets pitch dark inside so bring 2+ powerful flashlights. The cave entrance can be hard to find - watch where small rental boats go. Cave extends far back with rocks at the end of the main area, then zigzags deeper. Spectacular cliffs. No mobile network - perfect for a true escape. Daytime visit recommended for cave exploration; overnight stays possible with boat alone.<br>naziv: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Coordinates: 42° 57.55' N, 16° 0.98' E
Sea bed: Sand
Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW
Depth: ~15m

Incredible anchorage on Biševo island featuring the spectacular Medvidina špilja (Monk Seal Cave) - a real alternative to the crowded Blue Grotto with free entry! Anchor in about 15m on sand with turquoise water. Explore the very large, very deep cave by dinghy or paddle - it gets pitch dark inside so bring 2+ powerful flashlights. The cave entrance can be hard to find - watch where small rental boats go. Cave extends far back with rocks at the end of the main area, then zigzags deeper. Spectacular cliffs. No mobile network - perfect for a true escape. Daytime visit recommended for cave exploration; overnight stays possible with boat alone.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="naziv">
            <value/>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.0147062,42.9599463,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
