      <Placemark>
        <name>Samograd Bay</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Coordinates: 42° 58.50' N, 16° 59.70' E<br>Sea bed: Sand and Rocks<br>Wind Protection: Protected from E/SE; not well protected from Bura (N wind)<br>Depth: 6-7m<br><br>Wonderful anchorage bay on Korčula island with a small pebble beach. Anchor in 6-7m on sand, very close to the beach. Crystal clear, clean water. Pure nature setting with an incredible variety of butterflies! Very protected and calm with no swell when winds are from E/SE. Lines ashore possible to small beach. Often quiet with few or no other boats overnight. Caution: Not very deep bay so not necessarily well protected from Bura (north wind). Great for swim stops or overnight in light/favorable winds.<br>naziv: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Coordinates: 42° 58.50' N, 16° 59.70' E
Sea bed: Sand and Rocks
Wind Protection: Protected from E/SE; not well protected from Bura (N wind)
Depth: 6-7m

Wonderful anchorage bay on Korčula island with a small pebble beach. Anchor in 6-7m on sand, very close to the beach. Crystal clear, clean water. Pure nature setting with an incredible variety of butterflies! Very protected and calm with no swell when winds are from E/SE. Lines ashore possible to small beach. Often quiet with few or no other boats overnight. Caution: Not very deep bay so not necessarily well protected from Bura (north wind). Great for swim stops or overnight in light/favorable winds.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="naziv">
            <value/>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.9949001,42.974468,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Spomenik Posipa</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Coordinates: 42° 54.33' N, 16° 54.63' E<br>Sea bed: Sand and Seagrass (mixed Posidonia)<br>Wind Protection: Protected from S/SE; good protection under rock corner<br>Depth: 3-4m at the end<br><br>Isolated and wild mini-fjord on Korčula island facing S/SE - an amazing secluded experience! Space for only one yacht with lines ashore required. Beautiful clear water with access to a small beach (path leads up through olive trees and vineyards to the town of Zavalatica). Reef to the south excellent for diving/snorkeling. Very quiet spot - one of the highlights for many visitors. Caution: Lots of bees! Note: Beach itself can have bad smell from fish/burnt trash, but the walk inland is rewarding.<br>naziv: Point 99]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Coordinates: 42° 54.33' N, 16° 54.63' E
Sea bed: Sand and Seagrass (mixed Posidonia)
Wind Protection: Protected from S/SE; good protection under rock corner
Depth: 3-4m at the end

Isolated and wild mini-fjord on Korčula island facing S/SE - an amazing secluded experience! Space for only one yacht with lines ashore required. Beautiful clear water with access to a small beach (path leads up through olive trees and vineyards to the town of Zavalatica). Reef to the south excellent for diving/snorkeling. Very quiet spot - one of the highlights for many visitors. Caution: Lots of bees! Note: Beach itself can have bad smell from fish/burnt trash, but the walk inland is rewarding.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="naziv">
            <value>Point 99</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.9104748,42.9056641,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
