    <Folder>
      <name>Dag 10 og 11 - Mandag og Tirsdag</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Transport dag 10</name>
        <styleUrl>#line-0097A7-6425-nodesc</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            16.6912991,43.0892972,0
            16.4530331,43.154952,0
            16.3534695,43.1945113,0
            16.5292507,43.2360459,0
            16.5424687,43.2321689,0
          </coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Uvala Borova</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 5.02' N, 16° 43.37' E<br>Sea bed: Sand and Seagrass (caution: some areas rock with dust layer)<br>Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW<br>Depth: ~10m<br><br>Superb, magnificent bay on Hvar island with crystal-clear water. Very small - room for only 2-3 boats swinging, more with lines ashore. Quiet and uncrowded even in high summer. Anchor at 10m with ~35m chain on sand with shore line for good holding. Caution: Ground can be tricky - some areas appear sandy but are actually rock with a dust layer that won't hold. Look carefully for sandy patches and avoid seagrass. Excursion boats may visit around 10am. Wasps can be a significant problem!]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.7216745,43.083975,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Uvala Smokova</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 5.12' N, 16° 43.67' E<br>Sea bed: Sand and Seagrass<br>Wind Protection: Sheltered from N winds, but only partially protected<br>Depth: ~8m<br><br>Beautiful bay on Hvar island in the right conditions. Room for 3-4 boats. Anchor in 8m in a sand patch and back into the bay with lines ashore for a very secure mooring. Very quiet anchorage. Historical interest: 50-minute walk to restaurants (better to go to Portorusa for dining), but along the way you'll find 3 ancient anchors on display - one lead and wood from 1st century BC, another stone and wood from 2nd century BC. Well worth a visit!]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.7277926,43.0853521,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Uvala Nova Pošta</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 5.53' N, 16° 44.12' E<br>Sea bed: Sand<br>Wind Protection: Well protected from prevailing winds (N, NW)<br>Depth: 3-5m<br><br>Nice little secluded bay on Hvar island with room for 1 boat only (maybe 2 maximum). Turquoise blue water over good sandy bottom. Anchor with shore lines - in calm conditions one line may suffice, but add a second if current pushes the boat. Perfect for lovers of nature and calm - no facilities, no restaurants, no buoy fees. A great escape from the neighboring commercial bays.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.7352617,43.0922846,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Uvala Pribecica</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 5.65' N, 16° 43.67' E<br>Sea bed: Sand and Seagrass<br>Wind Protection: Protected from N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW<br>Depth: Not specified<br><br>Very protected and calm anchorage on Hvar island. Small bay with room for 1-2 boats with lines ashore. Beautiful very small beach around. Limited reviews available - a quiet, undiscovered spot.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.72762,43.0939812,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Store Stone Bay</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 5.67' N, 16° 43.03' E<br>Sea bed: Sand and Seagrass<br>Wind Protection: Very well protected from S winds<br>Depth: 9-10m<br><br>Beautiful quiet bay on Hvar island - often empty when neighboring bays have 5-6 boats. Anchor in 9-10m on sand with ~30m chain and two lines ashore - anchor holds very strong first time. Very clear water, lovely for swimming. Great stopover between Korčula and Hvar. Fantastic spot for a swim stop or overnight stay. No services - pure nature.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.7171944,43.0943237,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Uvala Rasohatika</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Coordinates: 43° 5.85' N, 16° 41.55' E<br>Sea bed: Sand, Rocks, and Seagrass<br>Wind Protection: Very well sheltered from wind and W swell<br>Depth: ~8m<br><br>Superb, very quiet and romantic bay on Hvar island - great for bathing and comfortable overnight stays. Anchor in ~8m on sandy bottom with shore lines to large rocks on the NW side. Room for about 6 boats. Caution: Rocks are razor-sharp when securing lines; anchor may need re-setting as holding can be tricky despite sandy appearance. Bonus: Philip the vendor visits by boat selling local schnapps, wine, honey, and takes bread/croissant orders for morning delivery - the honey is excellent and well-priced! Can handle Bora winds well, staying calm overnight.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1623-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            16.6924995,43.0970924,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
